# GATE 3 regression pin (issues/seed-built-stage1-array-fill-method-miss.md):
# `check` over a directory whose OWN prelude.yo is one of the checked targets.
# The walker reaches prelude.yo (sorted first) before zz_use.yo; the prelude
# was ALSO pre-loaded, so before the fix it was evaluated TWICE — TS died
# loudly on its duplicate-method check (whenever the pre-load and target keys
# differed: relative --std-path, or a symlinked prefix like macOS /tmp), and
# the self-hosted compiler silently corrupted the generic-impl registry so
# zz_use.yo's where-constrained Array specialization failed with "No matching
# call found". Red-first verified against both pre-fix compilers.
#
# stdout_keep_match: the self-hosted check prints extra progress chatter
# ("check: parsing ...") and the two compilers render file paths differently
# (absolute vs as-written), so the kept line is the verdict summary — which is
# exactly what the pin asserts.
stdout_keep_match=check: [0-9]+/[0-9]+ file\(s\) passed
timeout=120
